Subject: urdfdom_headers: include cstdint in model_state.h
Origin: DHI-internal (GCC 15 build of urdfdom_headers for the alpine leaf)
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/ros/urdfdom_headers.git af0f9306bcb6b88dcc79d75f28f6c5257c883bfd
Verify: cmd `ros2 run robot_state_publisher robot_state_publisher --help` expect "usage"
Forwarded: not-needed (upstream removed model_state.h on its main branch)
Drop-When: upstream >= 2.0.0

model_state.h declares int32_t members but includes only string, vector and map. GCC 15 no longer pulls cstdint in
through those headers, so urdfdom fails to compile against it with "int32_t does not name a type". Including cstdint
declares the fixed-width types the header already uses.

--- a/include/urdf_model_state/model_state.h
+++ b/include/urdf_model_state/model_state.h
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@
 #ifndef URDF_MODEL_STATE_H
 #define URDF_MODEL_STATE_H

+#include <cstdint>
 #include <string>
 #include <vector>
 #include <map>
